prompt:
Use the supplied Nova Stitch gameplay sprite as the identity/style reference. Create an original 1536×1024 transparent RGBA sheet with exactly eight distinct full-body Nova Stitch basketball-steal poses arranged in a four-column by two-row grid, row-major. All poses are right-facing at consistent scale and camera. Clear separate cells with broad transparent spacing. No court, floor, scene, shadow, glow, ball, hoop, text, labels, teammates or opponents.

Nova is a young athletic fair-tan woman with long curly teal hair tied in a high ponytail, an individual human face, teal jersey and shorts with purple/black trim, black knee pads, teal-and-black shoes and wristbands. Preserve her human anatomy, face, hair, silhouette and uniform colors. Hands stay empty; the game ball is a separate object and must never appear in the sprite poses.

Action: Nova anticipates an opponent’s dribble, darts in and steals the invisible ball with her right hand, then pivots to move away. Eight connected unique poses:
0 balanced defensive stance, knees bent, eyes ahead;
1 shift weight forward and extend the near hand;
2 quick side-step with shoulders turning toward the ball;
3 GRAB at simulation tick5: right arm reaches into the ball’s chest-height path and fingers close;
4 pull the empty hand back toward her ribs as possession changes;
5 pivot toward image-right, ponytail trails from the turn;
6 begin a quick escape step with the arms naturally counterbalancing;
7 regain a forward-facing running-ready pose.
Keep a readable one-hand interception and full athletic movement; no visible ball in any frame. Complete natural limbs, ponytail and shoes in every cell.

Match the tiny 2D arcade reference: crisp limited-palette 1990s pixel art with chunky dark outlines, not painterly, photoreal, 3D, glossy or anime. True alpha-zero background and gutters, no matte or checkerboard. Return only the sheet.
